{"name":"Pumpkin Pie Oh My!","hex":"#edc994","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pumpkin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A domesticated plant, in species Cucurbita pepo, similar in growth pattern, foliage, flower, and fruit to the squash or melon.","The round yellow or orange fruit of this plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pumpkin"},{"term":"pie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Piro."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of pastry that consists of an outer crust and a filling. (Savory pies are more popular in the UK and sweet pies are more popular in the US, so \"pie\" without qualification has different connotations in these dialects.)","Any of various other, non-pastry dishes that maintain the general concept of a shell with a filling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oh My!","blocks":[{"text":"Oh My! is an indiepop band from Sundsvall, Sweden. The band was formed in 2008 by the members of Second Hand Rumours and The Intrigues. In 2011 Oh My! signed with legendary indie label A West Side Fabrications and quickly released their first single Twenty One. Twenty one featured in the MTV Latin America series Niñas Mal and on Swedish national radio. Oh My! Has since that released three more singles which all feature on Swedish national radio. Time Will Tell even qualified for Hall of Fame in the competition \"Låtduellen\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Oh_My%21.jpg/330px-Oh_My%21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oh_My!","wikidata":"Q7080496"},{"title":"Pumpkin pie","blocks":[{"text":"Pumpkin pie is a dessert pie with a spiced, pumpkin-based custard filling. The pumpkin and pumpkin pie are both a symbol of harvest time, and pumpkin pie is generally eaten during the fall and early winter. In the United States and Canada it is usually prepared for Thanksgiving, Christmas, and other occasions when pumpkin is in season. Pumpkin is in season generally from mid-October through November. Harvest occurs during October which is just in time for Thanksgiving."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Pumpkin-Pie-Whole-Slice.jpg/330px-Pumpkin-Pie-Whole-Slice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pumpkin_pie","wikidata":"Q2118270"},{"title":"Pumpkin","blocks":[{"text":"A pumpkin is a cultivated winter squash in the genus Cucurbita. The term is most commonly applied to round, orange-colored squash varieties, but does not possess a scientific definition. It may be used in reference to many different squashes of varied appearance and belonging to multiple species in the Cucurbita genus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/FrenchMarketPumpkinsB.jpg/330px-FrenchMarketPumpkinsB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pumpkin","wikidata":"Q165308"},{"title":"Pie","blocks":[{"text":"A pie is a baked dish which is usually made of a pastry dough casing that contains a filling of various sweet or savoury ingredients. Sweet pies may be filled with fruit, nuts, fruit preserves, brown sugar, sweetened vegetables, or with thicker fillings based on eggs and dairy. Savoury pies may be filled with meat, eggs and cheese, or a mixture of meat and vegetables."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Top_down_view_of_peach_pie_%28722379748%29.jpg/330px-Top_down_view_of_peach_pie_%28722379748%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pie","wikidata":"Q13360264"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Recette_Tarte_citrouille_etape_1.jpg/500px-Recette_Tarte_citrouille_e